OSWP — Raglan Old School Arts Centre Website

WordPress site for a community arts centre. The site runs on a custom-built theme, referred to here as wpos — the site's own visual and functional system, purpose-built for this project. wpos is built on top of Forty, a design template by HTML5UP, which supplies the base CSS/JS/visual language; wpos is the actual integration — WordPress plumbing, content structure, and site- specific behaviour layered on top of Forty's design foundation. Content (events, pages) is managed through Advanced Custom Fields (ACF) and Custom Post Type UI (CPT UI).

Read this document top to bottom and you should be able to work on the site with no other context.

Stack
WordPress (via Docker: wordpress:latest + mysql:8.0)
PHP — theme templates, no build step, no compiler
wpos — the site's own theme (child theme, technically named oswp-child on disk — see Directory Structure below), built on Forty's CSS/JS foundation
Advanced Custom Fields (free tier) — all event/content data
Custom Post Type UI — registers the event post type and the venue / event_category / staff taxonomies
Code Snippets plugin — used for a small amount of ad-hoc PHP outside the theme (check before assuming all logic lives in functions.php)
Requirements to run locally
Docker + Docker Compose
WP-CLI is expected to be available inside the WordPress container for admin/content tasks (wp post, wp theme, etc.)
ImageMagick, if using the included image-prep scripts (imgprep.sh, imgaudit.sh — not part of the theme itself, dev utilities only)
bash
docker compose up -d

Site available at whatever port docker-compose.yml maps (historically :8080 locally).

